15:29.512 --> 15:31.221
If you could sum up the show
with one sound,

15:31.222 --> 15:32.556
what would it be?

15:32.557 --> 15:34.516
- "Blech."
- For me, it was more like

15:34.517 --> 15:36.852
the last squirt of
a plastic mustard bottle.

15:38.310 --> 15:39.688
<i>Is that our mustard?</i>

15:39.689 --> 15:42.732
No. I always bring one with me
in case the show is kind of...

15:44.068 --> 15:47.070
<i>- Everybody, shut up!
- Hey, it's that sheriff from The Q.</i>

15:47.071 --> 15:48.447
You people don't like anything.

15:48.448 --> 15:49.823
Well, if you're all so smart,

15:49.824 --> 15:52.200
<i>what do you want to see
in a Family Guy reboot?</i>

15:52.201 --> 15:54.911
Yes, unemployable neck tattoo guy.

15:54.912 --> 15:56.118
It's a Bible verse.

15:56.119 --> 15:57.838
Doesn't matter.
Anything above the Adam's apple

15:57.839 --> 15:58.915
means drugs.

15:58.916 --> 16:00.917
I like Netflix. Could you be Netflix?

16:00.918 --> 16:02.586
Yeah, Netflix is awesome.

16:02.587 --> 16:03.962
Of course it's awesome; it's Netflix.

16:03.963 --> 16:06.715
Look, we're stuck being Fox.
We have to deal with it, okay?

16:06.716 --> 16:09.176
- I watch Fox.
- No, you don't. Nobody does.

16:09.177 --> 16:11.261
Yeah, I like shows
that are binge-worthy.

16:11.262 --> 16:13.013
First of all,
"binge-worthy" is not a word,

16:13.014 --> 16:14.514
it's a marketing tool.

16:14.515 --> 16:16.308
You've been brainwashed, sir. But fine.

16:16.309 --> 16:19.269
<i>We'll make Family Guy binge-worthy.</i>

17:10.238 --> 17:12.088
See? Wasn't that terrible?

17:12.089 --> 17:14.282
All right, we only have the room
till 6:00, so what else?

17:14.283 --> 17:17.077
It's not 6:00 yet! What else?!

17:17.078 --> 17:20.038
<i>Young Sheldon is good.
How about Young Family Guy?</i>

17:20.039 --> 17:21.706
How about I murder your whole family?

17:21.707 --> 17:24.167
<i>- What about BoJack Horseman?
- Hard no.</i>

17:24.168 --> 17:26.378
- You'd get to be a horse.
- Hard yes.

17:26.379 --> 17:29.965
- Normal words, but a horse guy.
- Can we please stop this?

17:29.966 --> 17:31.925
You just asked for specifically that.

17:31.926 --> 17:34.469
It's not 6:00! What else?

17:34.470 --> 17:37.222
<i>- I like that Antiques Roadshow.
- Fine.</i>

17:37.223 --> 17:38.431
And you're saying this is...?

17:38.432 --> 17:39.849
George Washington's poop.
That's correct.

17:39.850 --> 17:41.851
I have some news you might not like.

17:41.852 --> 17:43.353
The poop is only two weeks old.

17:43.354 --> 17:44.896
What? How can you be sure?

17:44.897 --> 17:47.148
Well, for starters,
there's a Skittle in it.

17:47.149 --> 17:50.277
Ah, the general had a sweet tooth, huh?

17:50.278 --> 17:51.987
Um, that was horrible.

17:51.988 --> 17:53.321
Eh, I'm gonna tweeze the Skittle out

17:53.322 --> 17:54.489
and go back in a week.

17:54.490 --> 17:56.783
I like those Netflix stand-up specials.

17:56.784 --> 17:58.368
Great. Matter of fact, we filmed one

17:58.369 --> 18:01.538
back when I was an all-setup-
no-punch-line comedian.

18:01.539 --> 18:03.582
So, any of you out there have a futon?

18:03.583 --> 18:06.167
Yeah, yeah, right?

18:06.168 --> 18:07.919
I Ubered here tonight.

18:09.422 --> 18:11.881
Man, Starbucks.

18:11.882 --> 18:14.092
Facebook, huh?

18:14.093 --> 18:17.220
And how about that new chip
in credit cards?

18:17.221 --> 18:19.889
Anybody ever been to Georgia?

18:19.890 --> 18:21.933
The new iPhone is large.

18:23.561 --> 18:25.604
EDM music.

18:25.605 --> 18:27.230
Boo! You stink!

18:27.231 --> 18:30.859
Yeah! Dane Cook already
did all these halves of jokes.

18:30.860 --> 18:32.444
Hey, hey, this is my job.

18:32.445 --> 18:35.363
I don't go down to Burger King.

18:35.364 --> 18:36.573
That was terrible.

18:36.574 --> 18:38.867
Netflix should make 800 more of those.

18:38.868 --> 18:40.327
All right, what else?
What else you guys want?

18:40.328 --> 18:42.412
I like that thing James Corden does:

18:42.413 --> 18:44.457
<i>- Carpool Karaoke.
- I can do that.</i>

18:45.499 --> 18:47.667
Hi. You having a good night? I did.

18:47.668 --> 18:49.419
Just had a devil's three-way.

18:49.420 --> 18:51.004
You know, me and two guys.

18:51.005 --> 18:53.923
I think that's just gay sex.
Why are you telling me all this?

18:53.924 --> 18:55.884
<i>Isn't this Taxicab Confessions?</i>

18:55.885 --> 18:58.053
<i>No, this is Carpool Karaoke.</i>

18:58.054 --> 18:59.971
We're about to sing an Adele song.

18:59.972 --> 19:01.097
Oh, that's gay.

19:01.098 --> 19:03.266
Pull over by this hot guy
and let me out.

19:03.267 --> 19:06.227
I thought I read you guys
were phasing out gay jokes.

19:06.228 --> 19:08.104
That quote was taken out of context

19:08.105 --> 19:09.272
and widely misunderstood.

19:09.273 --> 19:10.815
All right, what's next, you sheep?

19:10.816 --> 19:13.443
I like the Olympics.
Can you guys be the Olympics?

19:13.444 --> 19:15.487
Well, NBC hogs all the good sports,

19:15.488 --> 19:17.197
so we'll get stuck with the boring ones

19:17.198 --> 19:19.991
that the announcers always
have to keep apologizing for.

19:19.992 --> 19:21.992
Welcome back to pairs diving.

19:21.993 --> 19:23.828
And once again,
we are so sorry for this.

19:23.829 --> 19:25.205
Brian, anything to add?

19:25.206 --> 19:28.041
No, just our deepest
condolences to a bored nation.

19:28.042 --> 19:29.459
And we've got Lois down at the pool.

19:29.460 --> 19:32.087
- Lois, anything?
- No. Guys, just so sorry

19:32.088 --> 19:33.421
that any of this is happening.

19:33.422 --> 19:35.507
I-I mean, even once every four years

19:35.508 --> 19:37.258
seems like just way too much.

19:37.259 --> 19:40.845
And they're up in the air,
and now they're in the water.

19:40.846 --> 19:43.139
What is it again? A splash is bad?

19:43.140 --> 19:44.724
Uh, yeah, I think so.

19:44.725 --> 19:46.267
That's so stupid.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.228
I'm sick of all the voices on your show.

19:48.229 --> 19:49.979
- Can you change them up?
- To who?

19:49.980 --> 19:51.648
I like Jon Benjamin voices.

19:51.649 --> 19:53.775
Can you all be Jon Benjamin voices?

19:53.776 --> 19:55.214
- Hey, Joe.
- Hey, Peter.

19:55.215 --> 19:57.904
- Hey, Quagmire.
- Hey, Cleveland. Giggity.

19:57.905 --> 19:59.989
What can I get for you fellas?

19:59.990 --> 20:03.034
<i>Nobody touches my voice.</i>

20:03.035 --> 20:04.494
I liked all of that.

20:04.495 --> 20:06.162
Um, except for the bartender.

20:06.163 --> 20:09.708
Hey, guys, The Coffee Bean's
Wi-Fi doesn't need a password.

20:09.709 --> 20:11.376
Everyone, the reboot is off.

20:11.377 --> 20:13.378
It turns out
the executive who ordered it

20:13.379 --> 20:15.714
was just a squirrel
who snuck into the office.

20:15.715 --> 20:17.340
- What?
- Yes. But in fairness,

20:17.341 --> 20:20.760
<i>it was the same squirrel who
green-lit Brooklyn Nine-Nine,</i>

20:20.761 --> 20:22.345
the show that challenged the notion

20:22.346 --> 20:25.098
that only attractive people
can be on television.

20:25.099 --> 20:27.058
So, what does that mean?

20:27.059 --> 20:30.478
<i>It means Family Guy
is just fine as it is.</i>

20:34.150 --> 20:36.526
<i>Well, the Family Guy reboot is off.</i>

20:36.527 --> 20:38.069
What other ideas do we have?

20:39.990 --> 20:41.948
<i>Brooklyn Nine-Ten?</i>

20:41.949 --> 20:45.161
It's possible
this guy only has one idea.

20:51.542 --> 20:53.543
You know what, I'm glad, after all that,

20:53.544 --> 20:55.587
they let us keep the show
the way it was.

20:55.588 --> 20:57.547
Well, not exactly the way it was.

20:57.548 --> 21:01.092
Hey, buddy, I brought over
my big band records.

21:01.093 --> 21:03.971
- They wanted more Joe.
- They wanted more Joe.

21:10.895 --> 21:13.354
<i>Your show should have more Joe Swanson.</i>

21:24.033 --> 21:26.409
<i>Your show should have more Joe Swanson.</i>